# Benchy — Architecture Rules

## Do not break architecture without discussion

- Keep the shell ↔ tool ↔ persistence model. Tools do not invent their own project file formats.
- Do not add a backend/API layer without an explicit design decision documented in `docs/design-decisions.md`.

## Follow established patterns

- Register tools in `toolRegistry.js`, `sidebarNav.js`, and `toolManifest.js`.
- Persist via `useToolSnapshot(instanceId, toolId, getSnapshot)` and shell autosave.
- Use `storageBackend` for KV/blobs — never hard-code only IndexedDB or only Electron store.
- Shared UI: `ToolHeader`, `LtTabs`, `ToolActionBar` from `src/shared/ui/`.

## Naming trap

- Tool id `qpcr-analyzer` → component from **`src/apps/qpcr-insight/`**.
- Do not recreate `src/apps/qpcr-analyzer/`.

## Explain architectural changes

When changing shell session lifecycle, `.benchy` schema, Electron IPC, or tool registration, update `docs/architecture.md` (and `docs/PERSISTENCE.md` / `docs/database-schema.md` if storage/formulas are involved).

## Electron security

Keep `contextIsolation: true` and `nodeIntegration: false`. Extend IPC only through `preload.cjs`.
